IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-time`

-- Section 9: Regulations.
-- Subsection (1) is the power to make regulations, for the seven purposes of paragraphs (a) to (g) (the type `Head of section 9(1)` in vmu-nouns).
-- Subsection (2) says when Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 does not apply, by what the Treasurer certifies in writing.
-- Subsections (3) to (5) say which roundings are deemed to be calculations in accordance with subsection (2).
-- The dates, the divisors (10 dollars, 100 dollars) and the roundings are in vmu-time.

§ `Section 9 -- Regulations`

-- "The Governor in Council, on the certificate and recommendation of the Treasurer, may make regulations amending any statutory rule made under any Act to—" the seven purposes.
-- The power is limited in its own words to those conditions and purposes; outside them the text says neither yes nor no, so NOTHING.
-- src:86 | (1) The Governor in Council, on the certificate and recommendation of the Treasurer, may make regulations amending any statutory rule made under any Act to—
-- src:87 | (a) convert any fees specified in monetary amounts in the statutory rule to fee units;
-- src:88 | (b) convert any penalties specified in monetary amounts in the statutory rule to penalty units;
-- src:89 | (c) convert any fee units or penalty units specified or referred to in the statutory rule to fee units or penalty units calculated in accordance with this Act;
-- src:90 | (d) convert the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit specified or referred to in the statutory rule to the equivalent monetary amount of that fee unit or penalty unit calculated in accordance with this Act;
-- src:91 | (e) convert any fee units specified in the statutory rule to fees specified in monetary amounts;
-- src:92 | (f) convert any penalty units specified in the statutory rule to penalties in monetary amounts;
@ref s 9(1), s 9(1)(a), s 9(1)(b), s 9(1)(c), s 9(1)(d), s 9(1)(e), s 9(1)(f) (src:86-92)
GIVEN `the regulation is made by the Governor in Council on the certificate and recommendation of the Treasurer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation amends a statutory rule made under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the regulation` IS A `Head of section 9(1)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` MEANS
    IF     `the regulation is made by the Governor in Council on the certificate and recommendation of the Treasurer`
       AND `the regulation amends a statutory rule made under an Act`
       AND `paragraphs (a) to (g) list the purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `paragraphs (a) to (g) list the purpose` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the purpose of the regulation`
            WHEN `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "(2) Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 does not apply to a regulation made under this section if the Treasurer certifies in writing that—".
-- The conversion certified must be the one that the paragraph names for the purpose of the regulation (paragraphs (a) to (h)),
-- and for purposes (a) and (b) it depends on whether the regulation takes effect on or before 1 July 2004 or after it.
-- src:94 | (2) Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 does not apply to a regulation made under this section if the Treasurer certifies in writing that—
-- src:95 | (a) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(a)—
-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
-- src:97 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:98 | (b) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:99 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by $100; or
-- src:100 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:101 | (c) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(c), the regulation converts fee units to the equivalent number of fee units having regard to the current value of a fee unit under this Act;
-- src:102 | (d) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(c), the regulation converts penalty units to the equivalent number of penalty units having regard to the current value of a penalty unit under this Act;
-- src:103 | (e) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(d), the regulation converts the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit specified or referred to in the statutory rule to the equivalent monetary amount of that fee unit or penalty unit under this Act;
-- src:104 | (f) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(e), the regulation converts fee units to fees in monetary amounts by multiplying the amount of the fee unit by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:105 | (g) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(f), the regulation converts penalty units to penalties in monetary amounts by multiplying the amount of the penalty unit by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:106 | (h) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(g), the regulation increases any fees that are less than the value of one fee unit by an amount not exceeding the cumulative annual rates fixed by the Treasurer under this Act for the period that the fee has had effect without any increase.
@ref s 9(2), s 9(2)(c), s 9(2)(d), s 9(2)(e), s 9(2)(f), s 9(2)(g) (src:94-106)
GIVEN `the purpose of the regulation` IS A `Head of section 9(1)`
      `the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` IS A `Conversion certified`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose of the regulation`
    -- (a) a regulation under subsection (1)(a): (i) on or before 1 July 2004, divide the fee by 10 dollars; (ii) after 1 July 2004, divide it by the value of a fee unit
    WHEN `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` THEN
        IF `s 9(2) -- the regulation takes effect on or before 1 July 2004` `the day on which the regulation takes effect`
        THEN `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `dividing the fee by 10 dollars`
        ELSE `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `dividing the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`
    -- (b) a regulation under subsection (1)(b): (i) on or before 1 July 2004, 100 dollars; (ii) after, the value of a penalty unit
    WHEN `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units` THEN
        IF `s 9(2) -- the regulation takes effect on or before 1 July 2004` `the day on which the regulation takes effect`
        THEN `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `dividing the penalty by 100 dollars`
        ELSE `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `dividing the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`
    -- (c) and (d) both name a regulation under subsection (1)(c): (c) for fee units, (d) for penalty units
    WHEN `converting fee units or penalty units to fee units or penalty units calculated in accordance with the Act` THEN
            `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `converting fee units to the equivalent number of fee units having regard to the current value of a fee unit`
        OR  `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `converting penalty units to the equivalent number of penalty units having regard to the current value of a penalty unit`
    -- (e) a regulation under subsection (1)(d)
    WHEN `converting the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit to the equivalent monetary amount calculated in accordance with the Act` THEN
        `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `converting the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit to the equivalent monetary amount under the Act`
    -- (f) a regulation under subsection (1)(e)
    WHEN `converting fee units to fees in monetary amounts` THEN
        `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `multiplying the amount of the fee unit by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`
    -- (g) a regulation under subsection (1)(f)
    WHEN `converting penalty units to penalties in monetary amounts` THEN
        `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `multiplying the amount of the penalty unit by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`
    -- (h) a regulation under subsection (1)(g)
    WHEN `increasing fees in monetary amounts by the cumulative annual rates` THEN
        `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` EQUALS `increasing fees less than the value of one fee unit by an amount not exceeding the cumulative annual rates`
    WHEN `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)` THEN FALSE

-- Paragraph (a) as a calculation: the number of fee units to which a regulation under subsection (1)(a) converts a fee in dollars.
-- On or before 1 July 2004 the divisor is 10 dollars; after it, the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3) (NOTHING if that value is 0, which divides nothing).
-- src:95 | (a) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(a)—
-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
-- src:97 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
@ref s 9(2)(a) (src:95-97)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(2)(a) -- the number of fee units to which the regulation converts the fee` MEANS
    IF `s 9(2) -- the regulation takes effect on or before 1 July 2004` `the day on which the regulation takes effect`
    THEN JUST (`s 9(2)(a)(i) -- the number of fee units when the fee is divided by 10 dollars` `the amount of the fee, in dollars`)
    ELSE `s 9(2)(a)(ii) -- the number of fee units when the fee is divided by the value of a fee unit` `the amount of the fee, in dollars` `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`

-- Paragraph (b) as a calculation: 100 dollars on or before 1 July 2004, the value of a penalty unit after.
-- src:98 | (b) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:99 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by $100; or
-- src:100 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
@ref s 9(2)(b) (src:98-100)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(2)(b) -- the number of penalty units to which the regulation converts the penalty` MEANS
    IF `s 9(2) -- the regulation takes effect on or before 1 July 2004` `the day on which the regulation takes effect`
    THEN JUST (`s 9(2)(b)(i) -- the number of penalty units when the penalty is divided by 100 dollars` `the amount of the penalty, in dollars`)
    ELSE `s 9(2)(b)(ii) -- the number of penalty units when the penalty is divided by the value of a penalty unit` `the amount of the penalty, in dollars` `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`

-- Part 2 does not apply "if the Treasurer certifies in writing that" the regulation makes the conversion the paragraph names.
-- "if" is the text's own condition: where it is not met, this subsection does not disapply Part 2, and the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- Whether Part 2 applies otherwise is not said here. For a purpose the paragraphs of subsection (1) do not list the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:94 | (2) Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 does not apply to a regulation made under this section if the Treasurer certifies in writing that—
@ref s 9(2) (src:94)
GIVEN `the Treasurer certifies in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the regulation` IS A `Head of section 9(1)`
      `the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the conversion the Treasurer certifies` IS A `Conversion certified`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) -- this subsection disapplies Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 to the regulation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose of the regulation`
    -- A regulation for a purpose that paragraphs (a) to (g) of subsection (1) do not list is not "a regulation made under this section": the text does not say.
    WHEN `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        JUST (    `the Treasurer certifies in writing`
              AND `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `the purpose of the regulation` `the day on which the regulation takes effect` `the conversion the Treasurer certifies`)

-- "(3) ... the number of fee units or penalty units is deemed to be calculated in accordance with those provisions if the fee unit or penalty unit is rounded up to the next 2 decimal places."
-- This subsection deems the number that results from rounding up the number calculated; any other stated number is not deemed by it (JUST FALSE).
-- src:107 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(a) and (b), in calculating the number of fee units or penalty units, the number of fee units or penalty units is deemed to be calculated in accordance with those provisions if the fee unit or penalty unit is rounded up to the next 2 decimal places.
@ref s 9(3) (src:107)
GIVEN `the number of units calculated by dividing under section 9(2)(a) or (b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of units the regulation states` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(3) -- the number of units the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(a) or (b)` MEANS
    JUST (`the number of units the regulation states` EQUALS `s 9(3) -- the number rounded up to the next 2 decimal places` `the number of units calculated by dividing under section 9(2)(a) or (b)`)

-- "(4) ... the amount of the fee is deemed to be calculated in accordance with that provision if the fee is rounded to the nearest 10 cents."
-- Where the amount calculated is exactly half way between two multiples of 10 cents, the text does not say which is "the nearest": NOTHING.
-- src:108 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2)(f), in calculating the amount of a fee, the amount of the fee is deemed to be calculated in accordance with that provision if the fee is rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
@ref s 9(4) (src:108)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee calculated under section 9(2)(f), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the fee the regulation states, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(4) -- the amount of the fee the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(f)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 9(4) -- the amount of the fee rounded to the nearest 10 cents` `the amount of the fee calculated under section 9(2)(f), in dollars`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rounded THEN JUST (`the amount of the fee the regulation states, in dollars` EQUALS rounded)

-- "(5) ... the amount of the penalty is deemed to be calculated in accordance with that provision if the penalty is rounded to the nearest dollar."
-- src:109 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2)(g), in calculating the amount of a penalty, the amount of the penalty is deemed to be calculated in accordance with that provision if the penalty is rounded to the nearest dollar.
@ref s 9(5) (src:109)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty calculated under section 9(2)(g), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the penalty the regulation states, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5) -- the amount of the penalty the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(g)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 9(5) -- the amount of the penalty rounded to the nearest dollar` `the amount of the penalty calculated under section 9(2)(g), in dollars`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rounded THEN JUST (`the amount of the penalty the regulation states, in dollars` EQUALS rounded)
